<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="headline">
<div><p class="eyebrow">FOR THE NEXT PRACTICE</p><h1 id="headline">A little more focus.<br /><em>Every practice.</em></h1><p class="lead">Keep reference videos, notes, and your own recordings together. Pick up where you left off, one piece at a time.</p><p class="family">For your own practice, or the time you spend helping your child.</p><a class="cta" href={appStore}>Download on the App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="availability">Free · iPhone &amp; iPad · English · iOS / iPadOS 18.5+</p></div>
<aside class="practice-loop" aria-label="A simple practice rhythm"><p class="small-label">A SIMPLE PRACTICE RHYTHM</p><div><span>01</span><p>Listen.<small>Return to a reference.</small></p></div><div><span>02</span><p>Remember.<small>Keep the detail that matters.</small></p></div><div><span>03</span><p>Play again.<small>Record a take. Hear the difference.</small></p></div><p class="loop-footer">A little practice, every day.</p></aside>
</section>
<section class="available" aria-labelledby="available-title"><p class="eyebrow">AVAILABLE IN THE APP TODAY</p><h2 id="available-title">Everything around the piece.<br />Kept with the piece.</h2><div class="features"><article><span class="number">01 / REFERENCE</span><h3>A starting point.</h3><p>Organize songs in practice playlists. Add reference videos from YouTube, Files, or Photos.</p></article><article><span class="number">02 / NOTES</span><h3>A detail to remember.</h3><p>Capture a written note or a voice note for the passage you want to revisit.</p></article><article><span class="number">03 / RECORDINGS</span><h3>A take to hear again.</h3><p>Record your practice audio, replay it, and share a take when you want feedback.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="preview" aria-labelledby="preview-title"><div class="preview-copy"><p class="preview-label">IN DEVELOPMENT · NOT IN THE APP STORE YET</p><h2 id="preview-title">A closer look at<br />practicing together.</h2><p>We’re working on a view for parents who sit alongside a young musician: score pages and reminders, close at hand.</p><p class="preview-note">This 24-second preview shows a real development build with synthetic score pages and sample notes. The current App Store version has a different interface and does not include this new workflow.</p><p class="video-help">Play the preview →<br /><small>Silent video with on-screen captions.</small></p></div><figure><video controls playsinline preload="none" width="1080" height="1920" poster="/music-mirror/assets/preview-poster.jpg" aria-label="24-second upcoming parent workflow preview. Not in the App Store yet."><source src="/music-mirror/assets/music-mirror-upcoming-preview.mp4" type="video/mp4" /><track default kind="captions" srclang="en" label="English" src="/music-mirror/assets/preview.vtt" /><a href="/music-mirror/assets/music-mirror-upcoming-preview.mp4">Download the upcoming preview video</a></video><figcaption>Development preview · Sample practice content</figcaption></figure></section>
<section class="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">YOUR PRACTICE, ON YOUR DEVICE</p><h2 id="privacy-title">No account to get started.</h2></div><div><p>Practice playlists, notes, imported media references, and recordings are stored locally on your device and are not sent to the developer.</p><p class="muted">External content, such as YouTube videos, uses the selected service and is subject to its privacy practices.</p><a href="/music-mirror/privacy.html">Read the privacy policy ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="closing" aria-label="Download Music Mirror"><h2>Make room for the next practice.</h2><a class="cta" href={appStore}>Download on the App Store <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><p class="availability">The current release: reference videos, notes, and practice recordings.</p></section>
